{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "20260908 Synthetic Forest Substation Cooling Controller Malfunction in High-Temperature Episode",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The first fan bank's start threshold in the temperature controller was retained at 92°C rather than 78°C.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The cooling control logic used an ambient bias that remained at zero when the outdoor temperature exceeded 43°C.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The hand-off-auto selector for the entire cooler group sat in manual without its lockwire.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A 6 A ground-fault current leaked into the analogue temperature input through old cable insulation; the leak was present for months before the trip.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Although ambient temperature was 47°C, this value alone was not the root cause; the transformer load was only 75 percent of rating.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A 40 MVA auxiliary transformer was taken out of service, raising the station load demand on the target transformer.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The step-down transformer's oil temperature increased from 88°C to 105°C during a 20-minute interval.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5, 0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The supervisor dispatched a remote start command to the oil pump at 14:56.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        },
        {
          "text": "The manual selector blocked this remote command; the pump did not energise.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7, 2]
        },
        {
          "text": "The leaked current shifted the reported top-oil temperature downward by 6°C continuously.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        },
        {
          "text": "The SCADA trend recorded 99°C, while a calibrated gauge at the transformer showed 105°C.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "Confident in the lower reading, the shift charge engineer reduced the alarm threshold to 103°C.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 15:04, the winding hot-spot relay operated and sent a trip signal to the transformer circuit breaker.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Synthetic Grid network lost 116 MW of firm supply when the 220 kV ring separated.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fourteen customers under the feeder experienced voltage dips between 31% and 45% for about 700 ms.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [13]
        },
        {
          "text": "The post-event oil sample displayed ethylene above 1100 ppm, indicating severe thermal stress.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the trip, two technicians manually closed the cooling valve and turned both pump switches to forced-run.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The control algorithms were replaced with the archived 2019 revision, resetting the start setpoint to 78°C.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Engineers repaired the cable insulation and recalibrated the analogue input card using a precision source.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer remained at 70% MVA load for 24 hours until all thermal indications returned to normal.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "20260908 Synthetic Riverside Substation Transformer 2 Cooling Controller Trip During Heat",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The cooling controller's integrator error was negative; valve reference fell while temperature rose.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The outdoor air sensor was mounted in a still pocket, far from the natural draft.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A 20 mm layer of dust insulated the cooling thermostat bubble from the pipe.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The dc battery voltage collapsed to 68 V for several seconds under unbalanced charging.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The day was hot, yet the 48.5°C peak was not the primary cause of the shutdown; load had been within 98% of planned limits.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A 55 kVA motor-driven pump started, reducing the oil level in the sump and triggering the low-level switch.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The control loop setpoint switched to cold reserve via an unbalanced automation state.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 17:11, the transformer protection saw a maximum winding temperature of 172°C.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5, 0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The inlet valve remained at its minimum stop, overruled by the negative integrator.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7, 0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The fan speed reduction forced the top-oil temperature to increase at a rate of 1.4 K per minute.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operators relied on the instantaneous analogue indication, ignoring the stale trend for 15 minutes.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The hot oil release continued past the rupture, and the safety valve began to chatter.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer relay detached the incoming feeder at 17:13 and isolated the faulty bay.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The synthetic local load received a 35% voltage drop for 1.8 seconds before the capacitor banks switched out.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Factory output at Synthetic Park stopped for 38 minutes after the low-voltage tripping.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [13]
        },
        {
          "text": "An oil leak of 25 litres formed, contaminating the concrete bund and raising environmental concern.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The operator manually opened the inlet valve using a 500 mm wrench after local confirmation.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Portable fans were directed at the radiator intake until the oil trend reached 70°C.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Control engineers ramped the integrator gain down to 0.1 and re-initialised the setpoint block.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer re-entered service after a six-hour stabilisation at 40 percent capacity.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
